  "systematic_insights": [
    "1. In both isotopes, the 3qp shears band undergoes a crossing around hbar*omega = 0.37 - 0.42 MeV driven by the alignment of a pair of g7/2 protons, creating a 5qp configuration.",
    "2. Crossing frequency and spin are shifted slightly between N=76 (135Pr, 0.37 MeV, 33/2-) and N=78 (137Pr, 0.42 MeV, 35/2-) due to the shifting Fermi level within the nu(h11/2) subshell.",
    "3. Prior to the crossing, both nuclei exhibit an increase in B(M1)/B(E2) ratios (from ~10-15 up to >60-95 (mu_N/eb)^2), proving that simplistic universal monotonic drop rules fail across bandcrossing regions.",
    "4. Above the crossing, 137Pr demonstrates the expected shears closing behavior of the 5qp configuration with B(M1)/B(E2) falling from 62.1 at 37/2- to 17.2 at 41/2-, whereas 135Pr lacks measured crossover E2 lines at high spin.",
    "5. Neither nucleus has measured DSAM/RDDS lifetimes for these bands; both remain candidate MR bands characterized by relative electromagnetic transition signatures."
  ],
